        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "28972886-e417-5f28-8c1d-640dca400ca6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Monica Bellucci, Mel Gibson, Benedict Fitzgerald, Jim Caviezel, Maia Morgenstern, Jan Kounen, Tchéky Karyo, Vincent Cassel, Georges de La Tour, Mary Magdalene, Jesus Christ, Virgin Mary, Persephone\n- Products: The Passion of the Christ, The Matrix Reloaded, The Matrix Revolutions, Malèna, Irréversible, Dobermann, Magdalene with the Smoking Flame\n- Concepts: biblical drama films, science-fiction films, French Baroque painting\n\nFacts:\n- In 1640, Georges de La Tour painted Magdalene with the Smoking Flame, an oil-on-canvas depiction of Mary Magdalene.\n- In 1997, Jan Kounen directed the French film Dobermann, which starred Tchéky Karyo, Vincent Cassel, and Monica Bellucci.\n- In 2000, Monica Bellucci played Malèna Scordia in the film Malèna.\n- In 2003, Monica Bellucci played Persephone in the science-fiction films The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix Revolutions.\n- In 2004, The Passion of the Christ was released as an American biblical drama film directed by Mel Gibson and written by Mel Gibson and Benedict Fitzgerald.\n- In 2004, The Passion of the Christ starred Jim Caviezel as Jesus Christ, Maia Morgenstern as the Virgin Mary, and Monica Bellucci as Mary Magdalene.\n- Monica Bellucci also played Alex in the art film Irréversible.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
